# Reset ChatGPT Desktop App Credentials (macOS, Terminal)

Run each step yourself. Steps 4–5 are irreversible — do step 3 first.

## 1. Confirm the bundle ID
```
osascript -e 'id of app "ChatGPT"'
```
Substitute whatever it returns for `com.openai.chat` below.

## 2. Quit the app
```
osascript -e 'quit app "ChatGPT"'
```

## 3. Inspect before deleting (non-destructive)
```
ls -la ~/Library/Application\ Support/com.openai.chat ~/Library/Preferences/com.openai.chat.plist ~/Library/Caches/com.openai.chat 2>/dev/null
security find-generic-password -s "ChatGPT" 2>/dev/null; security dump-keychain login.keychain-db 2>/dev/null | grep -i -B1 -A3 openai
```

## 4. Delete app data (irreversible — the actual reset)
```
rm -rf ~/Library/Application\ Support/com.openai.chat \
       ~/Library/Preferences/com.openai.chat.plist \
       ~/Library/Caches/com.openai.chat \
       ~/Library/Saved\ Application\ State/com.openai.chat.savedState
```

## 5. Remove stored token from Keychain
Run for each entry surfaced in step 3; adjust `-s` to the exact service name.
```
security delete-generic-password -s "ChatGPT" login.keychain-db
```

## 6. Reopen and sign in fresh
```
open -a ChatGPT
```

Notes:
- If step 1's bundle ID or step 3's Keychain service name differs, swap in the real values before running 4–5.
- The in-app route (Settings -> Account -> Log out) is cleaner if it works; use this only if logout is stuck or a full wipe is wanted.
